  "description": "Spacious Second-Floor 3-Bedroom Apartment with Underground Parking in Richmond Hall\nVR Property is delighted to present Apartment 10, Block 1, Richmond Hall, a bright and spacious first-floor 3-bedroom, 2-bathroom apartment located within this highly regarded gated development on Richmond Road, Dublin 3.\n\nExtending to approximately 92 sq.m., this well-proportioned apartment offers generous accommodation throughout, making it an excellent choice for both owner-occupiers and investors.\n\nThe property benefits from a designated underground parking space, secure gated access and well-maintained communal landscaped grounds. The generous living accommodation, three well-sized bedrooms and two bathrooms make this an ideal home for families, professionals or those looking for a spacious property close to Dublin City Centre.\n\nRichmond Hall – Excellent Dublin 3 Location\n\nRichmond Hall is a modern, secure gated development ideally positioned along the banks of the River Tolka, at the Fairview end of Richmond Road.\n\nThe development is within easy reach of Fairview Village, Drumcondra and Dublin City Centre, offering an excellent balance between convenient city living and access to green spaces and the coast.\n\nO'Connell Street is approximately 3 km away, while Drumcondra and Clontarf Road DART stations provide convenient access to the wider Dublin area.\n\nThere is also an excellent selection of local amenities nearby, including shops, cafés, restaurants, schools and recreational facilities. Fairview Park, Croke Park and Clontarf Promenade are all within easy reach.\n\nThe property also offers convenient access to the M1, M50 and Dublin Airport.\n\nAccommodation Comprises\n\nEntrance Foyer\nWelcoming entrance area providing access to the apartment and leading into the main hallway.\n\nHallway – 3.43m x 2.68m\nGenerous central hallway providing access to the living accommodation, bedrooms and bathrooms, with additional storage space.\n\nLiving/Dining Room – 6.83m x 3.58m\nA particularly spacious and bright open-plan living and dining area, providing excellent space for both relaxing and entertaining. The room benefits from plenty of natural light and views towards the communal grounds.\n\nKitchen – 2.90m x 2.44m\nWell-appointed fitted kitchen with a good range of wall and floor units and integrated appliances, including fridge-freezer, oven, hob, extractor fan and dishwasher.\n\nMaster Bedroom – 7.05m x 2.77m\nExceptionally spacious master bedroom featuring built-in wardrobes and access to a private en-suite shower room. The bedroom benefits from a brand-new carpet.\n\nBedroom 2 – 5.66m x 3.23m\nA generous double bedroom offering excellent floor space and built-in storage.\n\nBedroom 3 – 3.76m x 2.99m\nA well-proportioned third bedroom, also suitable as a double bedroom, guest room or home office.\n\nEn-Suite\nPrivate en-suite shower room serving the master bedroom.\n\nFamily Bathroom – 2.42m x 1.67m\nFully fitted bathroom comprising a bath, WC and wash-hand basin.\nLocation\n\nRichmond Hall enjoys a highly convenient location on Richmond Road, close to Fairview Village and within easy reach of Dublin City Centre.\n\nThe surrounding area provides a wide range of amenities, including supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, schools and leisure facilities. Fairview Park is nearby, while the Clontarf seafront and promenade are also easily accessible.\n\nFor commuters, the property's proximity to Drumcondra and Clontarf Road DART stations, along with numerous Dublin Bus routes, provides excellent connectivity throughout the city and beyond.\n\nThis is an excellent opportunity to acquire a spacious three-bedroom apartment in a secure and well-established development in Dublin 3. Early viewing is highly recommended.\n\nDisclaimer\n\nVR Property for themselves and for the vendors or lessors of this property whose agents they are, give notice that the particulars set out are for guidance only. Although every care is taken in preparing the details, they do not constitute any part of an offer or contract. Any intending purchaser should not rely on them as statements or representations of fact but should satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of the information provided. Measurements are approximate and photographs are for illustrative purposes only.",
